module

public import WeilConjectures.CategoryTheory.SmoothPurity.ProEtaleClosedCechPresentation

/-! # Exactness of the affine closed Cech presentation on the complementary open

Source: the matching-relations calculation in Steps 1--3 of
`lem-sp-proetale-closed-affine-cech-presentation-exact`.
-/

@[expose] public section
set_option autoImplicit false
universe u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
attribute [local instance] Over.ConstructProducts.over_finiteProducts_of_finiteWidePullbacks

/-- The affine closed Cech presentation is exact after restriction to the complementary open.

Source: Steps 1--3 of `lem-sp-proetale-closed-affine-cech-presentation-exact`.
(blueprint: lem-sp-proetale-closed-affine-cech-open-exact).

Proof: Use the retained affine lift presentation of each of the three degrees,
including its full relation cokernel, and restrict to the open complement.
Resolve the closed intersections by affine weakly contractible hypercovers;
the inverse-image evaluation formula identifies their generators with the
canonical henselian lifts. Refine the finite diagrams through degree q+2 by
principal-open and retained-localization covers, retaining all faces and all
equalities between composites. After restriction to the open, the pieces
outside the retained lifts contribute zero. On each remaining piece the
augmented lifted nerve is contracted by insertion of a chosen local lift.
Thus its kernels are generated by boundaries. The contraction respects the
retained relations, so descends through their cokernels. These local exactness
calculations imply exactness of the restricted sheaf complex. Naturality of
the representing equivalences identifies its boundaries with those of T.
The same contraction handles empty charts, and zero coefficients give zero
terms.
-/
theorem closedAffineCech_open_restriction_exact
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Finite A] {B O : Scheme.{u}}
    (b : O ⟶ B) [IsOpenImmersion b] [QuasiCompact b]
    (P : B.ProEt) (V : P.left.ProEt) (hV : IsAffine V.left)
    {n : ℕ} (U : Fin n → Over V)
    (hU : ∀ (k : ℕ) (y : Fin (k + 1) → Fin n),
      IsAffine (Presheaf.cechNerveObj U y).left.left)
    (hcover : Sieve.ofArrows (fun a ↦ (U a).left) (fun a ↦ (U a).hom) ∈
      ProEt.topology P.left V)
    (q : ℕ) (T : CochainCorepresentingShortComplex
      (closedCechCoefficientFunctor A b P V U) q) :
    (T.complex.map (ProEtale.upperStar
      (ModuleCat.{u + 1} (ULift.{u + 1, u} A)) b)).Exact := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
